{"tool_name":"normqpcr","contents":["bioconda","bioconductor","biotools","oeb"],"identifiers":["biotools:normqpcr","bioconductor:normqpcr","bioconda:bioconductor-normqpcr"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"normqpcr","home":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/NormqPCR","license":"LGPL-3.0","summary":"The package provides functions to read raw RT-qPCR data of different platforms.","addition_date":"2017-01-17T15:03:25Z","last_update_date":"2026-11-23T09:14:26.546677Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["1.58.0"],"collections":["BioConductor"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:normqpcr","credit":[{"name":"James Perkins"},{"name":"Matthias Kohl"},{"name":"Nor Izayu Abdul Rahman"}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/NormqPCR"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Nucleic acid design","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3095"},{"term":"Standardisation and normalisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3435"}]}],"name":"NormqPCR","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"bioconductor_import","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/1471-2164-13-296","metadata":{"abstract":"<h4>Background</h4>Measuring gene transcription using real-time reverse transcription polymerase chain reaction (RT-qPCR) technology is a mainstay of molecular biology. Technologies now exist to measure the abundance of many transcripts in parallel. The selection of the optimal reference gene for the normalisation of this data is a recurring problem, and several algorithms have been developed in order to solve it. So far nothing in R exists to unite these methods, together with other functions to read in and normalise the data using the chosen reference gene(s).<h4>Results</h4>We have developed two R/Bioconductor packages, ReadqPCR and NormqPCR, intended for a user with some experience with high-throughput data analysis using R, who wishes to use R to analyse RT-qPCR data. We illustrate their potential use in a workflow analysing a generic RT-qPCR experiment, and apply this to a real dataset. Packages are available from http://www.bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/ReadqPCR.htmland http://www.bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/NormqPCR.html<h4>Conclusions</h4>These packages increase the repetoire of RT-qPCR analysis tools available to the R user and allow them to (amongst other things) read their data into R, hold it in an ExpressionSet compatible R object, choose appropriate reference genes, normalise the data and look for differential expression between samples.","authors":[{"name":"Bennett DL"},{"name":"Dawes JM"},{"name":"Kohl M"},{"name":"McMahon SB"},{"name":"Orengo C"},{"name":"Perkins JR"}],"citationCount":211,"date":"2012-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"BMC genomics","title":"ReadqPCR and NormqPCR: R packages for the reading, quality checking and normalisation of RT-qPCR quantification cycle (Cq) data."},"pmcid":"PMC3443438","pmid":"22748112"}],"topic":[{"term":"Genetics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3053"},{"term":"PCR experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3519"}],"validated":1},"bioconductor":{"name":"NormqPCR","version":"1.58.0","license":"LGPL-3","summary":"Functions for normalisation of RT-qPCR data","description":"Functions for the selection of optimal reference genes and the normalisation of real-time quantitative PCR data.","home":"www.bioconductor.org/packages/release/bioc/html/NormqPCR.html","author":"Matthias Kohl, James Perkins, Nor Izayu Abdul Rahman","maintainer":"James Perkins <jimrperkins@gmail.com>","bioc_views":["GeneExpression","MicrotitrePlateAssay","Software","qPCR"],"git_url":"https://git.bioconductor.org/packages/NormqPCR","last_commit_date":"2026-04-28"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:normqpcr:1.20.0/cmd/bioconductor.org","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribu